<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaels</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gaels are the Gaelic-speaking peoples of Ireland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and the Isle of Man, who share a common origin in early medieval Ireland. From the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, Gaelic language and culture spread through Scotland, and the merging of Gaels and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> in the 9th century produced the kingdom of Alba. Gaelic survives today as Irish, Scottish Gaelic and Manx.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaels.jpg" alt="Gaels" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CelticBrain · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Gaels.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
